# Everything here is optional: install.sh works with no .env at all. To override a default, put the line in
# .env (or pass it on the command line, which wins). install.sh appends what it generates (admin password,
# callback URL) to .env. The HolmesGPT bootstrap .env is a DIFFERENT file: PMM renders it into the shared
# config dir; you never write that one by hand.

# ADRE-capable PMM Server image. The official percona/pmm-server:3 does NOT include ADRE — use a Feature
# Build of the tibi-holmes branch.
# PMM_IMAGE=perconalab/pmm-server-fb:PR-4259-16e7b4f

# HolmesGPT image, >= 0.36.0 (native HTTPS + /api/admin/reload); targets 0.45.0. Pin a digest for prod.
# HOLMES_IMAGE=robustadev/holmes:0.45.0

# PMM admin password. Generated (and saved here) when unset.
# PMM_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Add an LLM during install. All three or none; without them, add the model in
# PMM → AI Assistant Deployment → Models & Keys. MODEL_NAME is the display/key name (letters, digits, .-_ only);
# LITELLM_MODEL is the LiteLLM model id. Prefer passing LLM_API_KEY on the command line over storing it here.
# MODEL_NAME=gpt-4.1
# LITELLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-4.1
# LLM_API_KEY=

# Optional cheaper model for Fast chat (questions and lookups); MODEL_NAME then serves Investigation mode only.
# FAST_LLM_API_KEY defaults to LLM_API_KEY (set it when the fast model is from another provider).
# FAST_MODEL_NAME=claude-sonnet
# FAST_LITELLM_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5
# FAST_LLM_API_KEY=

# The PMM URL HolmesGPT calls back on. It must be reachable from the Holmes container AND from browsers
# (answers embed panel image links). Default: https://<this host's IP>, else https://pmm-server:8443.
# PMM_CALLBACK_URL=https://pmm.example.com

# Host dir shared with the containers (certs + PMM-rendered Holmes config).
# HOLMES_CONFIG_DIR=./holmes-config
# Docker invocation if your user needs sudo (install.sh auto-detects).
# DOCKER=sudo docker
